Streaming tool execution for DSH 0.2.0-rc.2

This source is vendored from @teddybear/dsh-streaming-tool-execution 0.2.0-rc.2
(MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Te-ddybear).

It is a plugin port of the agent-loop change
"feat(agent-loop): execute parallel-safe tool calls while streaming":
Te-ddybear/deepseek-harness@de079108d2dcbef687ab6457b2bb7987fb67d292

The platform-local package is named mindagent-dsh-streaming-tool-execution.
Local changes: the package name, a repository field, a `peerDependencies` entry
pinning `@deepseek-ai/dsh` to 0.2.0-rc.2 (so DSH refuses a mismatched install
unless an explicit risk exemption is granted), and adding this NOTICE to the
`files` list so provenance travels with the packed tarball.

One runtime change is applied on top of upstream. Upstream imports
`@deepseek-ai/dsh-tools` and `@deepseek-ai/schemastery` by bare specifier and
exports a schemastery `Config`. A copy installed into a profile cannot resolve
those packages, so it failed to import with ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND unless it was
also installed inside the DSH installation itself. This copy imports nothing
from the host: it finds the scheduler symbol by its description
`@deepseek-ai/dsh-tools.scheduler` on the `tools` service, and reads
`streamingToolExecution` as a plain boolean instead of a schemastery schema
(no defaulting and no volatile remount semantics). Installation into the image
and the build-time checks are maintained in MindAgent-Platform.

